Paragraph 2: "Without loss of generality, we adapt the epsilon-greedy approach [42]. Define ε ≤1 as the exploration probability. We flip a coin with probability ε in each iteration and choose to explore or exploit based on this trial result. Let f' be the best-known solution with the maximum skew so far while considering a hyper-parameter τ' for the cosine similarity of the exploitation phase. During each exploration step, we draw random directions in the space of all possible directions. On the other hand, during the exploitation, we select the best-known direction f' and select a random direction from the space of possible direction in the τ-vicinity of f', defined as {f(s)|cos(f',f(s)) ≤ τ'}. This problem can be reduced to the problem of sampling uniformly from the surface of a unit d-dimensional spherical cone with the center f' and the angular radius of τ. We use the sampling approach proposed in [8]."

